<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation (Mammalian secondary hard palate (Mus musculus E12.0-E15.5 & Equus caballus Rugae palatinae))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-4> ;
    schema:about "Mammalian secondary hard palate (Mus musculus E12.0-E15.5 & Equus caballus Rugae palatinae)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element simulation of epithelial invagination with large deflections or nonlinear growth; calibrated ridge heights; emergence of the coronal-cut / bead / cyclopamine phenotypes from identical initial conditions (they are seeded by condition-specific initial patterns at L606-633); mechanics-dependent phenotypes compared with a published mechanical perturbation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2x2 Jacobian and dispersion relation with lambda_c = 3.2221; 1D and 2D RD solvers with growth-zone envelope; 9-stage L/lambda_c intercalation count; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG segmentation of the specimen shelves (15 / 16 rugae); Pass 3: quasi-static Kirchhoff plate on a Winkler foundation driven by beta max(A, 0), solved exactly by DCT-II, optional chi_m feedback, ridge count / phase-offset / duty-cycle morphometrics, kappa / k_f / chi_m sweeps, 2 Lean 4 theorems on the transfer stiffness",
        "reported_in_source: Economou et al. (2012): mesenchymal FGF10/FGF7 (activator) and epithelial SHH (inhibitor) form a Turing reaction-diffusion system at the rugae growth zone anterior to ruga 8; rugae are added sequentially 8 -> 1..7b as the palate elongates; a coronal explant cut across the growth zone yields bifurcations / spots whereas a sagittal cut preserves stripes; cyclopamine broadens and FGF10 beads / Spry2-/-;Spry4+/- compact the pattern; Shh expression marks each morphological ruga (Fig. 1)",
        "reported_in_source: Landau & Lifshitz (1986): equilibrium equation of a thin elastic plate and its bending stiffness",
        "reported_in_source: Pantalacci et al. (2008), Welsh & O'Brien (2009): staging of sequential ruga addition in the RGZ anterior to ruga 8",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability of a two-component activator-inhibitor system",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2D RD solver integrates on a rescaled x spacing dx_eff = dx (q / 1.24), so the realised grid wavelength (3.37) differs from the dispersion lambda_c (3.22) that Panels B / D use; the plate solver uses the physical dx",
        "transfer_boundary: The plate constants kappa = 0.05, T = 0.2, k_f = 1, beta = 1 are dimensionless modelling assumptions (no offline-verifiable measurement of embryonic palatal epithelial stiffness); only the sign-preservation, wavelength-transfer and monotone-attenuation predictions are scored, not ridge heights in micrometres",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen is an adult horse palate photograph; its duty cycle (0.49 / 0.44) is compared qualitatively with the simulated mouse-embryo ridges (0.42) after the same peak_widths estimator; DoG smoothing broadens the specimen crests" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Mus musculus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
