<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: exact FGF-SHH Jacobian, dispersion curve and equal-diffusion control (L183-237); 9-stage intercalation (L240-291); 2D growing-shelf RD with incision barriers (L516-737); and the new Law 4 plate coupling that is mathematically correct and exactly solved (transfer stiffness L391-402, DCT solver L405-429 certified against the FD operator L440-454, rectified thickening load L457-465, in-loop feedback L645-647 and L684-688), with 5 Lean theorems (0 sorrys). Deductions: the coronal-cut, FGF10-bead and cyclopamine outcomes are seeded by condition-specific initial patterns (mediolateral cos modulation and q_gz at L606-615, q_high + bead halo at L616-627, q_cyc at L628-633) so those phenotypes are not emergent consequences of the barrier or rate change (-5); the x spacing is rescaled by dx_eff = dx (q / 1.24) (L338, L600, L619, L631), decoupling the integrated wavelength (3.37) from the dispersion lambda_c (3.22) and from the plate's physical dx (-3); the plate is a linear 2.5D reduction with assumed dimensionless constants and one-way coupling by default (chi_m = 0), not the 3D FEM invagination requested (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L598–L600: dx_eff = dx * (q_ap / 1.24) rescaling: grid wavelength 3.37 vs dispersion lambda_c 3.22 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L598-L600>",
        "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L606–L633: Condition-specific initial conditions encode the coronal / bead / cyclopamine outcomes rather than letting them emerge <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L606-L633>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 14 reference-anchored measurements (L1429-1590): the 9 Pass 2 metrics plus mechanical ridge count (9 vs 9), crest/Shh-stripe phase offset (0.0226 vs 0 lambda), crest duty cycle against a value measured on the vendored specimen with the same estimator (0.423 vs 0.493; right shelf 0.444), kappa-sweep Spearman rho (-1.00 vs -1) and chi_m-sweep count robustness (9.0 vs 9). Deductions: three Pass 2 reference values remain self-referential (coronal bifurcation 0.4695 at L1545 and specimen CV 0.1843 at L1585 are the script's own outputs; in-phase r = 0.96 at L1515 is an eyeballed figure value) (-5); ridge amplitude is dimensionless so no height comparison with histology exists (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
