<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Source and data traceability: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five vendored files are SHA-256 pinned (L111-130) and verified fail-closed at every load (L141-167), including the new `palate_ridge_mechanics_reference.json` whose provenance block states plainly that the plate constants are modelling assumptions; the dataset README documents the fifth file and the thin-plate reference; the four primary DOIs are unchanged. Deductions: the Landau & Lifshitz entry has no DOI and its URL could not be verified offline during this run (-3); no measured palatal epithelial stiffness is cited for kappa, T, k_f (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The comparison PNG keeps the segmented specimen (Panel F, 15 / 16 rugae with detected crests) beside the 2D PDE, and Panel A now overlays the plate ridge crests (white contours) on the WT / coronal split view. The new ridge-mechanics PNG adds a 3D elevation surface of 9 transverse ridges (Panel A), a WT vs coronal elevation map with visibly fragmented ridges below the cut (Panel E), a flat equal-diffusion control at the same colour scale (Panel F) and a direct crest duty-cycle comparison with both specimen shelves (Panel D: 0.423 vs 0.493 / 0.444, sinusoid 0.5). Deductions: the specimen is an adult horse palate photographed at a different scale from the modelled mouse embryo (-4); simulated ridges are straight transverse bars whereas the specimen rugae are curved and the modelled arch phase (L603-604) is barely visible (-3); ridge heights are dimensionless so no height-to-spacing aspect ratio is compared (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

