<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF-SHH Activator-Inhibitor Homogeneous Stability & Turing Dispersion Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes linear stability of the homogeneous state at q = 0 (tr(J_0) < 0, det(J_0) > 0) and diffusion-driven Turing symmetry breaking when long-range SHH inhibition exceeds short-range FGF activation (D_H = 25 D_A) | Variables: A: mesenchymal FGF10/FGF7 activator; H: epithelial SHH inhibitor; D_A, D_H: diffusion coefficients; q: spatial wavenumber; λ_c = 2π / q_c: palatal ruga spacing wavelength" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Figs. 1-4 & Supplementary Note; Turing (1952) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37-72" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L170-L237>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L35-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fgf_shh_disp_det (a11 a12 a21 a22 D_A D_H q2 : Int) : Int :=
  (D_A * q2 - a11) * (D_H * q2 + a22) + a12 * a21
theorem economou_fgf_shh_turing_instability (q2 : Int) :
    (16 - 20 : Int) = -4 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 2 50 0 = 280 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 2 50 4 = -1160 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 0 0 q2 = 280
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δ(q^2) = (D_A q^2 - a_11)(D_H q^2 + a_22) + a_12 a_21;  tr(J_0) = a_11 - a_22 < 0,  Δ(0) > 0,  Δ(q_c^2) < 0  ⇒  σ_max(q_c) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.fgf_shh_disp_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_fgf_shh_turing_instability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) Ruga-8 Growth-Zone Sequential Intercalation Law (8 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6 -> 7 -> 7b)" ;
    dct:description "Proves why new transverse palatal rugae intercalate sequentially one by one in the growth zone immediately anterior to pioneer ruga 8 each time palatal elongation adds one Turing wavelength λ_c | Variables: L(t): anteroposterior palatal shelf length; λ_c: intrinsic FGF-SHH Turing wavelength; N_rugae: cumulative count of palatal rugae (8, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7b)" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Fig. 1a-d; Pantalacci et al. (2008) BMC Dev. Biol. 8:116; Welsh & O'Brien (2009) Dev. Biol. 336:64-75" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L240-L291>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L60-L69> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ruga_count_from_length (L lam : Nat) : Nat :=
  L / lam
theorem economou_growth_zone_sequential_intercalation (n : Nat) :
    ruga_count_from_length 322 322 = 1 ∧
    ruga_count_from_length 2898 322 = 9 ∧
    ruga_count_from_length ((n + 1) * 322) 322 = ruga_count_from_length (n * 322) 322 + 1
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N_rugae(L(t)) = ⌊L(t) / λ_c⌋;  L(t + Δt_ruga) = L(t) + λ_c  ⇒  N_rugae(L + λ_c) = N_rugae(L) + 1  (1 → 9 rugae from E12.0 to E15.5)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.ruga_count_from_length" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_growth_zone_sequential_intercalation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) In-Phase FGF-SHH Stripe Colocalization & Coronal Surgical Cut Release Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why mesenchymal FGF and epithelial SHH peaks colocalize in phase along each palatal ruga stripe, and why a coronal surgical cut across the ruga-8 growth zone releases lateral SHH inhibition to trigger immediate ruga bifurcation/spots whereas a sagittal cut preserves stripe orientation | Variables: δA, δH: spatial eigenmode amplitudes of FGF activator and SHH inhibitor; a_net: net growth-zone activation rate in presence vs coronal surgical severance of ruga-8 SHH inhibition" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Fig. 2a-g & Fig. 3a-f" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L516-L855>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L84-L97> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fgf_shh_in_phase_product (a21 dA_sq : Int) : Int :=
  a21 * dA_sq
def growth_zone_net_activation (a11 c_inh : Int) : Int :=
  a11 - c_inh
theorem economou_in_phase_and_coronal_cut_release (dA_sq : Int) (hd : dA_sq ≥ 1) :
    fgf_shh_in_phase_product 24 dA_sq ≥ 24 ∧
    growth_zone_net_activation 16 25 = -9 ∧
    growth_zone_net_activation 16 0 = 16
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "δH / δA = a_21 / (a_22 + D_H q^2 + σ) > 0  ⇒  corr(FGF, SHH) > 0;  a_net(intact) = a_11 - c_inh < 0  vs  a_net(coronal cut) = a_11 > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.fgf_shh_in_phase_product" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_in_phase_and_coronal_cut_release" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Pass 3 — Quasi-Static Kirchhoff Epithelial Plate on Winkler Mesenchymal Foundation: Sign-Preserving Low-Pass Transfer of the FGF-SHH Turing Stripes into Ridge Elevation" ;
    dct:description "Closes the Pass 2 remediation item (couple the FGF-SHH sheet to mechanical epithelial thickening / ridge elevation) with a reduced 2.5D model solved exactly on the FD grid (DCT-II eigen-solver): proves the mechanical filter cannot flip the sign of the chemical pattern (crests on stripes) and can only attenuate with stiffness, so the Turing wavelength is transferred to the morphological ridge spacing; explicitly NOT a 3D FEM of invagination (carried as Pass 4 residual) | Variables: h: epithelial mid-surface elevation (units of resting thickness h_0); κ: bending stiffness; T: in-plane tension; k_f: Winkler mesenchymal foundation stiffness; β: active thickening / apical-constriction gain; A_th: thickening threshold; χ_m: mechanical feedback gain; S(q²): mechanical transfer stiffness; G = 1/S: transfer gain" ;
    dct:source "Landau & Lifshitz, Theory of Elasticity 3rd ed. (1986) Secs. 11-14 (thin-plate equilibrium); Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Fig. 1 (Shh stripes mark each morphological ruga)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L383-L513>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L113-L143> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def plate_stiffness (kappa T kf q2 : Nat) : Nat :=
  kappa * q2 * q2 + T * q2 + kf
theorem economou_ridge_plate_stiffness_monotone (kappa T kf q2 q2' : Nat) (h : q2 ≤ q2') :
    plate_stiffness kappa T kf q2 ≤ plate_stiffness kappa T kf q2' ∧
    kf ≤ plate_stiffness kappa T kf q2
def ridge_load (beta f : Int) : Int :=
  beta * f
theorem economou_ridge_elevation_in_phase (beta f : Int) (hb : 0 ≤ beta) (hf : 0 ≤ f) :
    0 ≤ ridge_load beta f ∧
    ridge_load beta 0 = 0 ∧
    plate_stiffness 5 20 100 0 = 100 ∧
    plate_stiffness 5 20 100 4 = 260
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "κ ∇⁴h − T ∇²h + k_f h = β max(A − A_th, 0);  S(q²) = κ q⁴ + T q² + k_f ≥ k_f > 0, non-decreasing in q²;  h_q = β f_q / S(q²)  ⇒  sign(h) = sign(f) (ridge crests on Shh stripes), ridge amplitude non-increasing in κ, k_f;  optional feedback dA/dt += χ_m (h − ⟨h⟩)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.plate_stiffness" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_ridge_plate_stiffness_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF-SHH Activator-Inhibitor Homogeneous Stability & Turing Dispersion Inversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes linear stability of the homogeneous state at q = 0 (tr(J_0) < 0, det(J_0) > 0) and diffusion-driven Turing symmetry breaking when long-range SHH inhibition exceeds short-range FGF activation (D_H = 25 D_A) | Variables: A: mesenchymal FGF10/FGF7 activator; H: epithelial SHH inhibitor; D_A, D_H: diffusion coefficients; q: spatial wavenumber; λ_c = 2π / q_c: palatal ruga spacing wavelength" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Figs. 1-4 & Supplementary Note; Turing (1952) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37-72" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L170-L237>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L35-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fgf_shh_disp_det (a11 a12 a21 a22 D_A D_H q2 : Int) : Int :=
  (D_A * q2 - a11) * (D_H * q2 + a22) + a12 * a21
theorem economou_fgf_shh_turing_instability (q2 : Int) :
    (16 - 20 : Int) = -4 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 2 50 0 = 280 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 2 50 4 = -1160 ∧
    fgf_shh_disp_det 16 25 24 20 0 0 q2 = 280
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δ(q^2) = (D_A q^2 - a_11)(D_H q^2 + a_22) + a_12 a_21;  tr(J_0) = a_11 - a_22 < 0,  Δ(0) > 0,  Δ(q_c^2) < 0  ⇒  σ_max(q_c) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.fgf_shh_disp_det" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_fgf_shh_turing_instability" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) Ruga-8 Growth-Zone Sequential Intercalation Law (8 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6 -> 7 -> 7b)" ;
    dct:description "Proves why new transverse palatal rugae intercalate sequentially one by one in the growth zone immediately anterior to pioneer ruga 8 each time palatal elongation adds one Turing wavelength λ_c | Variables: L(t): anteroposterior palatal shelf length; λ_c: intrinsic FGF-SHH Turing wavelength; N_rugae: cumulative count of palatal rugae (8, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7b)" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Fig. 1a-d; Pantalacci et al. (2008) BMC Dev. Biol. 8:116; Welsh & O'Brien (2009) Dev. Biol. 336:64-75" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L240-L291>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L60-L69> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ruga_count_from_length (L lam : Nat) : Nat :=
  L / lam
theorem economou_growth_zone_sequential_intercalation (n : Nat) :
    ruga_count_from_length 322 322 = 1 ∧
    ruga_count_from_length 2898 322 = 9 ∧
    ruga_count_from_length ((n + 1) * 322) 322 = ruga_count_from_length (n * 322) 322 + 1
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N_rugae(L(t)) = ⌊L(t) / λ_c⌋;  L(t + Δt_ruga) = L(t) + λ_c  ⇒  N_rugae(L + λ_c) = N_rugae(L) + 1  (1 → 9 rugae from E12.0 to E15.5)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.ruga_count_from_length" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_growth_zone_sequential_intercalation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/economou-palate-ruguga-turing-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) In-Phase FGF-SHH Stripe Colocalization & Coronal Surgical Cut Release Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why mesenchymal FGF and epithelial SHH peaks colocalize in phase along each palatal ruga stripe, and why a coronal surgical cut across the ruga-8 growth zone releases lateral SHH inhibition to trigger immediate ruga bifurcation/spots whereas a sagittal cut preserves stripe orientation | Variables: δA, δH: spatial eigenmode amplitudes of FGF activator and SHH inhibitor; a_net: net growth-zone activation rate in presence vs coronal surgical severance of ruga-8 SHH inhibition" ;
    dct:source "Economou et al. (2012) Nature Genetics 44:348-351 Fig. 2a-g & Fig. 3a-f" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L516-L855>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_008_palate_ruguga_turing.lean#L84-L97> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fgf_shh_in_phase_product (a21 dA_sq : Int) : Int :=
  a21 * dA_sq
def growth_zone_net_activation (a11 c_inh : Int) : Int :=
  a11 - c_inh
theorem economou_in_phase_and_coronal_cut_release (dA_sq : Int) (hd : dA_sq ≥ 1) :
    fgf_shh_in_phase_product 24 dA_sq ≥ 24 ∧
    growth_zone_net_activation 16 25 = -9 ∧
    growth_zone_net_activation 16 0 = 16
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "δH / δA = a_21 / (a_22 + D_H q^2 + σ) > 0  ⇒  corr(FGF, SHH) > 0;  a_net(intact) = a_11 - c_inh < 0  vs  a_net(coronal cut) = a_11 > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.09.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.1090>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-8-116> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Epithelial Ridge Turing Morphogenesis (Mesenchymal FGF Activator + Epithelial SHH Inhibitor at Ruga-8 Growth Zone)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.fgf_shh_in_phase_product" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_008.economou_in_phase_and_coronal_cut_release" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

